    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1486" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀδρίας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀδρίης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εω</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the Adriatic</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				5.9
			</span></i>, etc.:— Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀδρι-ᾱνός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				71
			</span></i>, also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδραν-ηνός</span></b> , 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῦμα τᾶς Ἀδριηνᾶς ἀκτᾶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					736
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): later, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδραν-ακός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέκταρ</span>, of
			Italian wine, called <u>Adriatic</u> because imported
			through Corcyra, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.257
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>):</div>
